/-- **`cor:remainder_norms`** (Two remainder norms).

Write `D_{λ,r} = C_α λ^{37} R(r)^{21}`.  Then
`|R_T(F)| ≤ D_{λ,r} |Q_T| ∏_{j ∈ J} M_{T,4}(F_j)`. -/
theorem cor_remainder_norms (α : Anisotropy) :
    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 ≤ C ∧ ∀ (T : FiniteConvexTree α) (lam r : ℝ)
      (F : CubeVertex → E3 → ℝ),
      (∀ j, Continuous (F j)) →
      (∀ j, ∃ B : ℝ, 0 ≤ B ∧ ∀ y, |F j y| ≤ B) →
      1 ≤ lam →
      |cubeTreeRemainder α T lam r F| ≤
        C * lam ^ 37 * translationWeight r ^ 21 *
          (∏ j : CubeVertex, treeLocalSize T 4 (F j)) * boxMass α T.root :=
  cubeTreeRemainder_bound_of_boundedContinuous α

/-- **`lem:cube_cs`** (Cubical Cauchy--Schwarz and positivity).

For real bounded continuous tuples,
`|Θ^{(i)}_T(F)|^2 ≤ Θ^{(i)}_T(C_i^0 F) Θ^{(i)}_T(C_i^1 F)`.

This is the Cauchy--Schwarz half. -/
theorem lem_cube_cs_cauchySchwarz
    (α : Anisotropy) (S : BoxCollection α) (i : Fin 3) (lam r : ℝ)
    (F : CubeVertex → E3 → ℝ)
    (hFcont : ∀ j, Continuous (F j))
    (hFbound : ∀ j, ∃ C : ℝ, 0 ≤ C ∧ ∀ y, |F j y| ≤ C)
    (hlam : 1 ≤ lam) :
    |localCubeForm α S i lam r F| ^ 2 ≤
      localCubeForm α S i lam r (cubeCoordinateCopy i false F) *
        localCubeForm α S i lam r (cubeCoordinateCopy i true F) :=
  localCubeForm_cauchySchwarz α S i lam r F hFcont hFbound hlam

/-- **`lem:cube_cs`** (Cubical Cauchy--Schwarz and positivity).

`Θ^{(i)}_T(C_i^b F) ≥ 0`.

This is the positivity half. -/
theorem lem_cube_cs_nonneg
